<section class="s" id="roadmap"><div class="wrap">
<h2>What needs a backend</h2>
<p class="sub">This page is the public, no-account front end. Some features in the full NEXORA plan cannot be done honestly in a static page.</p>
<details><summary>Accounts, profiles and synced progress</summary><div>Registration, login and cross-device sync need a server and database with secure authentication. Today, favorites, saved prompts and lesson progress are stored in your browser only.</div></details>
<details><summary>Admin dashboard and moderation</summary><div>Publishing, user-submission review and analytics must be protected by server-side roles, not hidden buttons. They are not included here.</div></details>
<details><summary>Community and live AI responses</summary><div>A community needs moderation, guidelines and privacy controls. Live AI features need an API key held on a server. Until those exist, the Lab is a template builder, not an AI.</div></details>
<details><summary>News and fast-changing information</summary><div>This page shows no news feed on purpose. A curated editorial workflow with real dates and authors is required first.</div></details>
</div></section>

